1
00:00:00,303 --> 00:00:02,203
(Bernadette:)But it's weird... Howie's the one
who's been talking about

2
00:00:02,205 --> 00:00:03,635
(Bernadette:)having kids for years, and I was

3
00:00:03,639 --> 00:00:06,069
(Bernadette:)all excited to tell him because
I thought he'd be thrilled,

4
00:00:06,075 --> 00:00:07,845
(Bernadette:)but then he started to flip out

5
00:00:07,844 --> 00:00:09,714
(Bernadette:)and now this
feels like a bad idea

6
00:00:09,712 --> 00:00:12,712
(Bernadette:)and I'm gonna get fat.

7
00:00:12,715 --> 00:00:14,445
(Penny:)No, no, come on. Come on,
you're not gonna get fat.

8
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,120
(Penny:)You're gonna be beautiful
and glowing

9
00:00:16,119 --> 00:00:18,519
and-and have the cutest
little baby bump ever.

10
00:00:18,521 --> 00:00:20,791
(Bernadette:)Easy for you to say,
skinny bitch.

11
00:00:22,625 --> 00:00:24,595
(Bernadette:)Sorry, hormones.

12
00:00:24,594 --> 00:00:26,664
(Penny:)Oh, that's all right.
All I heard was "skinny."

13
00:00:27,563 --> 00:00:29,963
(Amy:)I wouldn't make too much
out of Howard

14
00:00:29,966 --> 00:00:31,696
(Amy:)not reacting the way
you expected him to.

15
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:32,739
(Penny:)Yeah, I'm sure

16
00:00:32,735 --> 00:00:34,335
(Penny:)it was just
the initial shock of it all.

17
00:00:34,337 --> 00:00:36,507
(Bernadette:)You're probably right.

18
00:00:36,506 --> 00:00:39,176
(Bernadette:)After we talked about it,
he started to calm down.

19
00:00:39,175 --> 00:00:40,905
(Howard:)I shouldn't be raising a kid.

20
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:43,110
(Howard:)I don't even
eat my own vegetables.

21
00:00:44,313 --> 00:00:46,543
Buddy, I-I think
you might be overreacting.

22
00:00:46,549 --> 00:00:48,449
(Howard:)And then there's
this nose.

23
00:00:48,451 --> 00:00:51,521
(Howard:)I mean, what if he
looks like me?

24
00:00:52,788 --> 00:00:53,988
(Howard:)Or worse...

25
00:00:53,990 --> 00:00:56,490
what if she looks like me?

26
00:00:56,492 --> 00:00:57,992
(Sheldon:)Not to mention

27
00:00:57,994 --> 00:00:59,994
(Sheldon:)the impact on our social circle.

